 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Totally normal fear. Many people never get past it. Would you rather ride where you lead a car every day, or on quieter roads that someone else clears for you? Commuting is different. You' usually on quieter roads, and there are usually fewer cars on them. Start with weekday lunchtime trips, and build up from there. Also, try to ride with someone else at first if you can. shared experience can make you feel much safer. Most bike clubs are shut down right now, but there are still pairs available on some routes. Ask at your local bike shop, or check social media for local groups.",
